const HELP_POL={"verification": {"title": "Provider verification", "html": "<p>Effective date: 8 November 2026</p>\n<p>Customers book strangers to come into their homes, so Kodu checks every provider before they can be booked. This policy explains what we check, how long it takes and what the badges on a profile mean.</p>\n<h2>1. What we check</h2>\n<table>\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th>Check</th>\n<th>Who needs it</th>\n<th>How we check</th>\n<th>Result on the profile</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td>Identity</td>\n<td>Every provider</td>\n<td>Photo of an Estonian ID card, residence permit card or EU passport, plus a live selfie, checked by our identity partner ID partner</td>\n<td>Verified ID badge</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Business details</td>\n<td>Companies (OÜ) and sole traders (FIE)</td>\n<td>Registry code checked in the Estonian e-Business Register</td>\n<td>Company name shown</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Trade qualification</td>\n<td>Trades where Estonian law requires one, such as electrical work and gas work</td>\n<td>Professional certificate checked in the Estonian qualifications register (Kutseregister) or the register of economic activities (MTR)</td>\n<td>Licensed badge</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>VAT number</td>\n<td>Providers registered for VAT</td>\n<td>Number checked in the EU VIES service</td>\n<td>VAT shown on receipts</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Liability insurance</td>\n<td>Optional, recommended for every trade</td>\n<td>Certificate uploaded and checked for cover dates and amount</td>\n<td>Insured badge</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table>\n<p>Providers can create an account, set up their profile and send quotes while checks are in review. Customers can only book and pay a provider once the identity check has cleared.</p>\n<h2>2. How long it takes</h2>\n<p>Most identity checks finish within minutes. Licence and insurance checks are done by a person and usually take up to 24 hours on working days. Providers see the status of each check in their profile.</p>\n<h2>3. When a check fails</h2>\n<p>We tell the provider which check failed and why, for example a blurred photo, an expired document or a certificate that does not match the name on the ID. The provider can upload a new document at any time. After three failed identity attempts the account is reviewed by our team before another attempt is allowed.</p>\n<h2>4. Keeping checks current</h2>\n<ol>\n<li>We store the expiry date of every document and remind the provider 30 days before it runs out.</li>\n<li>An expired licence removes the Licensed badge and hides the provider from searches for that trade until a new certificate is checked.</li>\n<li>An expired insurance certificate removes the Insured badge.</li>\n<li>We may ask any provider to verify their identity again, for example after a change of phone number, bank account or name, or if we see signs that someone else is using the account.</li>\n</ol>\n<h2>5. What badges do not mean</h2>\n<p>Badges show that a document was valid when we checked it. They are not a guarantee of the quality of the work. Reviews, photos of past work and the reliability score help customers judge that.</p>\n<h2>6. Removal from Kodu</h2>\n<p>We suspend or remove a provider who gives false documents, lets another person work under their account, asks customers to pay outside Kodu, or seriously breaks the Community Guidelines. The provider receives a statement of reasons and can ask us to review the decision, as set out in the Provider Agreement.</p>\n<h2>7. Data we keep</h2>\n<p>Identity documents are processed by our identity partner and Kodu keeps only the result of the check, the document type and its expiry date. Details are in the Privacy Notice.</p>"}, "guidelines": {"title": "Community guidelines", "html": "<p>Effective date: 8 November 2026</p>\n<p>Kodu brings together people from many countries who often do not share a language. These guidelines apply to everyone who uses Kodu: customers, providers and anyone working for a provider.</p>\n<h2>1. Be respectful</h2>\n<ol>\n<li>Treat everyone with courtesy, in chat, in reviews and at the door.</li>\n<li>No harassment, threats, insults or discrimination based on nationality, language, ethnicity, religion, gender, sexual orientation, disability or age.</li>\n<li>Remember that messages are machine translated. If something sounds rude, ask before assuming it was meant that way.</li>\n</ol>\n<h2>2. Be honest</h2>\n<ol>\n<li>Describe the job accurately and add photos when you can.</li>\n<li>Providers quote honestly and only for work they are qualified to do.</li>\n<li>Use your real name and your own account. Do not let anyone else work under your profile.</li>\n<li>Reviews describe your own experience of a real job.</li>\n</ol>\n<h2>3. Keep payments on Kodu</h2>\n<ol>\n<li>All payments go through Kodu, including extra work, which is added with a change order in the app.</li>\n<li>Asking for or offering cash, bank transfers or other payments outside Kodu is not allowed. It removes the escrow protection for the customer and the payment guarantee for the provider.</li>\n<li>Sharing phone numbers, emails or payment details in chat before a booking is paid is blocked automatically. Kodu provides a masked phone number once the job is booked.</li>\n</ol>\n<h2>4. Keep each other safe</h2>\n<ol>\n<li>Providers arrive at the booked time or message through Kodu if they are late.</li>\n<li>Providers respect the customer's home, clean up after the job and take photos of the finished work.</li>\n<li>Customers make sure the provider can reach the work area safely and tell them about hazards such as pets, asbestos or exposed wiring.</li>\n<li>If you ever feel unsafe, leave the situation and call 112. Then report it to Kodu.</li>\n</ol>\n<h2>5. Not allowed on Kodu</h2>\n<ol>\n<li>Illegal work, or work that needs a licence the provider does not hold.</li>\n<li>Fake profiles, fake reviews or paying for reviews.</li>\n<li>Offensive, sexual or violent content in profiles, photos or chat.</li>\n<li>Spam, scams and links that try to collect passwords or payment details.</li>\n<li>Using Kodu to find customers or providers and then moving the work off the platform.</li>\n</ol>\n<h2>6. Reporting</h2>\n<p>Use Report on any profile, message or review. A person reviews every report, usually within one working day, and we tell you what we decided and why. Reports are confidential: the other person is not told who reported them.</p>\n<h2>7. What happens when someone breaks the rules</h2>\n<p>Depending on how serious and how repeated it is, we may send a warning, remove content, limit the account, hide a provider from search, or close the account. Every decision comes with a statement of reasons and can be appealed through the help centre within six months.</p>"}, "payments": {"title": "Payments, cancellations and refunds", "html": "<p>Effective date: 8 November 2026</p>\n<h2>1. How payment works</h2>\n<ol>\n<li>The customer pays the full total when booking: labour, materials and the Kodu service fee of 10 percent.</li>\n<li>Payments are processed by our licensed payment partner, Stripe Payments Europe . Kodu never stores full card numbers.</li>\n<li>The money is held in escrow. It is released to the provider when the customer confirms the job is done, or automatically 72 hours after the booked visit if no problem has been reported.</li>\n<li>Providers are paid out every Monday, or the same day with instant payout for a small fee.</li>\n</ol>\n<h2>2. Fixed price services</h2>\n<p>Providers can publish a menu of standard jobs at a fixed price, such as replacing a tap cartridge. Customers book and pay these straight away without a quote. The fixed price includes labour. If the provider finds that materials or extra work are needed, they use a change order.</p>\n<h2>3. Materials deposits</h2>\n<p>For jobs with expensive parts, a provider can ask for the cost of materials as a deposit. The quote shows this clearly before the customer pays. The materials amount is paid to the provider when the customer books, so the parts can be bought before the visit. Labour and the rest of the total stay in escrow as usual. If the job is cancelled by the provider, the customer gets the deposit back in full. If the customer cancels after the parts were bought, the provider may keep the deposit and hand over the parts.</p>\n<h2>4. Change orders</h2>\n<p>If a job turns out bigger than quoted, the provider sends a change order in the app with the extra amount, a reason and a photo. The customer approves or declines it. Approved amounts are added to escrow with the Kodu fee. If the customer declines, the provider finishes the original job at the quoted price, or both sides can agree to cancel with a fair refund. Work done without an approved change order is not paid through Kodu and cannot be charged later.</p>\n<h2>5. Cancellation policies</h2>\n<p>Each provider chooses one of three policies. It is shown on their profile and on the payment screen before the customer pays.</p>\n<table>\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th>Policy</th>\n<th>Free cancellation</th>\n<th>Late cancellation fee</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td>Flexible</td>\n<td>Until 24 hours before the visit</td>\n<td>€15 call out fee</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Moderate</td>\n<td>Until 48 hours before the visit</td>\n<td>25 percent of the job</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Strict</td>\n<td>Until 72 hours before the visit</td>\n<td>50 percent of the job</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table>\n<p>The late cancellation fee goes to the provider. Everything else is refunded. A request that has not been paid yet can always be cancelled for free.</p>\n<h2>6. No shows</h2>\n<ol>\n<li>If the provider does not arrive within 30 minutes of the slot without messaging, the customer can cancel for a full refund and the provider's reliability score drops.</li>\n<li>If nobody lets the provider in and the customer does not reply within 30 minutes, the provider can mark a no show and keeps the late cancellation fee of their policy.</li>\n</ol>\n<h2>7. When a provider cancels</h2>\n<p>The customer gets a full refund, including any materials deposit, and we help them find another provider. Providers who cancel often lose ranking in search and may be suspended.</p>\n<h2>8. Refunds</h2>\n<p>Refunds go back to the original payment method and usually arrive within 5 working days. Partial refunds agreed in a dispute are shown in the job and on the receipt. Customers who are consumers keep their legal rights, including the right of withdrawal described in the Terms of Service.</p>"}, "disputes": {"title": "Dispute resolution", "html": "<p>Effective date: 8 November 2026</p>\n<p>If something goes wrong with a job, the payment stays protected while both sides are heard.</p>\n<h2>1. Reporting a problem</h2>\n<p>The customer can report a problem from the booking at any time before the payment is released, which is up to 72 hours after the visit. Reasons include: the provider did not show up, the job is not finished, poor quality, being charged more than the quote, or damage to the home. The customer describes the problem and adds photos. Reporting puts the payment on hold straight away.</p>\n<h2>2. Timeline</h2>\n<table>\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th>Step</th>\n<th>Time</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td>Provider is notified and can reply with their side and photos</td>\n<td>Within 48 hours</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Both sides can agree a solution in the app: the provider comes back to fix it, or offers a partial refund</td>\n<td>Any time</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>If there is no agreement, a Kodu specialist reviews the evidence</td>\n<td>Within 5 working days</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Decision with a written explanation sent to both sides</td>\n<td>Same day as the review</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table>\n<h2>3. Evidence we look at</h2>\n<ol>\n<li>The job description, the quote and any approved change orders.</li>\n<li>The chat, in both the original language and the translation.</li>\n<li>Photos from the customer, and the provider's before and after photos, which are required when marking a job as done.</li>\n<li>Arrival and completion times recorded in the app.</li>\n</ol>\n<h2>4. Possible outcomes</h2>\n<ol>\n<li>Release the payment to the provider in full.</li>\n<li>Ask the provider to return and fix the work at no extra cost, with the payment released after the fix is confirmed.</li>\n<li>Partial refund to the customer, with the rest released to the provider.</li>\n<li>Full refund to the customer.</li>\n</ol>\n<p>Damage to the home that costs more than the job is handled between the customer and the provider, or through the provider's liability insurance. Kodu shares the contact details needed to make a claim.</p>\n<h2>5. Appeals</h2>\n<p>Either side can ask for a second review by a different specialist within 14 days of the decision. After that, consumers can contact the Estonian Consumer Disputes Committee, and providers can use the mediation route set out in the Provider Agreement. Using Kodu's process never removes anyone's right to go to court.</p>\n<h2>6. Fair use</h2>\n<p>Opening disputes in bad faith, for example to avoid paying for work that was done, can lead to account limits. Providers are not penalised for disputes that are decided in their favour.</p>"}, "reviews": {"title": "Reviews and ratings", "html": "<p>Effective date: 8 November 2026</p>\n<h2>1. Who can leave a review</h2>\n<p>Only customers who booked and paid through Kodu can review a provider, and only after the job is finished. Each job allows one review, within 30 days. Reviews are written in the customer's language and translated for every reader, with the original available.</p>\n<h2>2. What a review shows</h2>\n<p>A rating from one to five stars, optional tags such as On time or Tidy work, optional text, the customer's first name and initial, the language they wrote in, and the date.</p>\n<h2>3. Provider replies</h2>\n<p>Providers can reply publicly to any review once, in their own language. The reply is translated for readers and shown under the review. Replies must follow the Community Guidelines: no personal details about the customer and no threats or insults. Providers can edit their reply.</p>\n<h2>4. Private customer ratings</h2>\n<p>Providers rate customers privately after each job. These ratings are never shown to customers or other providers. Kodu uses them to spot customers who repeatedly cause problems, such as no shows or abusive behaviour, and reviews those accounts.</p>\n<h2>5. How the overall rating is worked out</h2>\n<p>The rating on a profile is the average of all reviews from the last 24 months. Search ranking also uses reliability (on time arrival and few cancellations), reply time, distance and language match, as described in the Terms of Service.</p>\n<h2>6. Removing reviews</h2>\n<p>We do not remove a review because it is negative. We remove a review only if it breaks the Community Guidelines, is about a different job or person, contains personal data, or was written in exchange for payment or under pressure. Providers can report a review, and a person decides within 5 working days with a written explanation.</p>"}};
const HELP_FAQ={"expat": [["Getting started", [["What is Kodu?", "Kodu connects people living in Estonia with verified local tradespeople for plumbing, electrical work, painting, cleaning, handyman jobs and moving. You can search by the languages a provider speaks, chat with automatic translation and pay safely through escrow."], ["Which cities does Kodu cover?", "Tallinn, Tartu, Narva, Pärnu, Kohtla-Järve, Viljandi, Rakvere, Maardu, Kuressaare and Võru. You can filter by city and then by district."], ["Do I need to speak Estonian?", "No. Write in your own language and the provider reads it in theirs. You can also filter for providers who speak your language at B2 level or better."]]], ["Booking", [["How do I book a provider?", "Open a profile, tap Request quote, describe the job, add photos and pick a time slot. The provider replies with a written quote. You pay only when you accept it."], ["What is a fixed price service?", "Some providers list standard jobs at a fixed price, such as replacing a tap cartridge. You can book and pay these straight away, without waiting for a quote."], ["My landlord pays for repairs. Can Kodu handle that?", "Yes. Add your landlord's contact details in your profile. The quote is sent to them for approval before you can pay, and they never see your chat."], ["Can I book the same provider again?", "Yes. Tap Book again on a finished job, or save providers with the star on their profile."]]], ["Payment", [["When do I pay, and is my money safe?", "You pay when you accept a quote. The money is held in escrow by our payment partner, not sent to the provider. It is released when you confirm the job is done, or automatically 72 hours after the visit if you do not report a problem."], ["What does Kodu charge?", "A service fee of 10 percent, shown in every quote before you pay. There are no hidden costs."], ["What is a materials deposit?", "For jobs with expensive parts, the provider can ask for the cost of the materials when you book, so they can buy the parts before the visit. The quote shows this clearly. The rest stays in escrow until the job is done."], ["The provider says the job is bigger than quoted. What happens?", "They send a change order in the app with the extra amount, a reason and a photo. You decide whether to approve it. Never pay extra in cash."], ["How do I pay?", "By card, Apple Pay or Revolut. Kodu never stores your card number."]]], ["Cancelling and problems", [["Can I cancel a booking?", "Yes. Each provider has a Flexible, Moderate or Strict cancellation policy, shown on their profile and before you pay. Cancelling before the free cancellation deadline gives a full refund. After it, a late fee goes to the provider."], ["Something went wrong with the job. What do I do?", "Open the booking and tap Report a problem before the payment is released. The payment is put on hold, the provider has 48 hours to reply, and if you cannot agree, a Kodu specialist decides within 5 working days."], ["When will I get my refund?", "Refunds usually reach your card or account within 5 working days."]]], ["Trust", [["How do you check providers?", "Every provider who can be booked has had their identity verified. We also check licences for trades that need one, VAT numbers and, where uploaded, liability insurance. See the Provider Verification policy for details."], ["When does the provider see my address?", "They see your district when you send a request, and your full address only after you pay."], ["How accurate is the translation?", "Translation is automatic and works well for everyday messages, but it can miss technical terms. The original message is always shown under each translation. If something is unclear, ask, or send a photo."]]]], "provider": [["Joining", [["What do I need to join?", "A phone number, a photo ID, your trade, the areas you cover and a bank account for payouts. Companies also add their registry code and, if registered, their VAT number."], ["How long does verification take?", "The identity check usually takes minutes. Licence and insurance checks take up to 24 hours on working days. You can set up your profile and send quotes while you wait. Customers can book you once your ID is checked."], ["Does it cost anything to join?", "No. Kodu charges the customer a 10 percent service fee on each job. You receive the full amount of your quote."]]], ["Getting work", [["How do customers find me?", "By trade, city, district, language, availability and price. Ranking uses your rating, reliability, reply time, distance and language match. A complete profile ranks higher."], ["What is the profile strength score?", "A checklist in your profile: a profile photo, an about text, three photos of your work, an insurance certificate, at least three fixed price services and verified ID. Profiles above 80 percent get up to three times more requests."], ["Should I add a service menu?", "Yes, for standard jobs. Customers can book menu items instantly at your fixed price, so you get paid bookings without writing quotes."], ["What do Insights show?", "Quote acceptance, reply time, profile views, demand by district, your price against the area average, the busiest times and the most requested jobs, with suggestions to get more work."]]], ["Quotes and jobs", [["What kinds of quotes can I send?", "A fixed price, a price range with a maximum, or a paid site visit first. You can save quotes as templates and ask the customer a question before quoting."], ["Can I ask for materials up front?", "Yes. Turn on Ask for materials as a deposit in the quote. You receive the materials amount when the customer books."], ["What if the job turns out bigger than quoted?", "Tap Job is bigger than quoted and send a change order with the extra amount, a reason and a photo. Wait for the customer's approval in the app before you start the extra work."], ["I cannot make the requested time. Do I have to decline?", "No. Suggest another time from your free slots instead."], ["Why must I add photos when I finish a job?", "An after photo is required when you mark a job as done. Before and after photos protect you if the customer later reports a problem."]]], ["Getting paid", [["When do I get paid?", "When the customer confirms the job, or automatically 72 hours after the visit if they do not report a problem. Payouts go to your bank account every Monday, or the same day with instant payout."], ["What happens if a customer cancels late?", "You keep the late cancellation fee of the policy you chose: €15 on Flexible, 25 percent of the job on Moderate, or 50 percent on Strict."], ["Do I get receipts for my accounting?", "Yes. Every job has a printable receipt, and you can download a statement of your earnings. Kodu reports annual earnings over €2,000 to the Tax and Customs Board under the DAC7 rules."]]], ["Reviews and safety", [["Can I reply to reviews?", "Yes, once per review, publicly and in your own language. Kodu translates your reply."], ["What if a customer is difficult?", "Rate customers privately after each job. Only Kodu sees these ratings. You can also report a customer at any time, and if you ever feel unsafe, leave and call 112."], ["What if a customer opens a dispute?", "You have 48 hours to reply with your side and photos. You can offer to come back and fix it, offer a partial refund, or explain why the work was done as quoted."]]]]};
/* Help centre: FAQ for both sides and the trust and safety policies */
SCREENS.help=()=>{const tab=S.helpTab||(S.role==="provider"?"provider":"expat");const pk=S.helpPol||"verification";
 const tabs=[["expat","For expats"],["provider","For providers"],["policies","Safety and policies"]];
 const faq=tab==="policies"?"":HELP_FAQ[tab].map(([sec,qs])=>`<div class="col hsec" style="gap:8px"><b style="font-family:Sora,sans-serif;font-size:17px">${sec}</b><div class="card" style="padding:0 16px">${qs.map(([q,a])=>`<details class="hq"><summary>${q}<span class="hchev">${ico("plus","#16201D",18)}</span></summary><p>${a}</p></details>`).join("")}</div></div>`).join("");
 const pol=tab==="policies"?`<div class="row lchips" style="gap:8px;overflow-x:auto;margin:0 -20px;padding:0 20px">${Object.entries(HELP_POL).map(([k,v])=>`<button class="chip ${k===pk?"on":""}" data-hpol="${k}">${v.title}</button>`).join("")}</div><article class="legaldoc"><h1>${HELP_POL[pk].title}</h1>${HELP_POL[pk].html}</article>`:"";
 return `<div class="row" style="gap:10px;height:48px"><button class="ib" data-go="back" aria-label="Back">${ico("back")}</button><b style="font-family:Sora,sans-serif;font-size:18px">Help centre</b></div>
<div class="col" style="gap:4px"><h2>How can we help?</h2><p class="sub">Answers for expats and providers, and the rules that keep Kodu safe.</p></div>
<div class="segm">${tabs.map(([k,l])=>`<button class="${tab===k?"on":""}" data-htab="${k}">${l}</button>`).join("")}</div>
${tab==="policies"?"":`<div class="in"><span style="display:inline-flex">${ico("search","#56605C",20)}</span><input name="hq" placeholder="Search questions, for example refund" autocomplete="off"></div><p class="muted hnone" style="display:none">No questions match. Try another word, or write to us below.</p>`}
${faq}${pol}
${tab==="policies"?"":`<div class="card row" style="gap:10px;align-items:flex-start"><span class="eic" style="width:36px;height:36px;border-radius:11px;flex-shrink:0">${ico("shield","#16201D",18)}</span><span style="flex:1"><b style="font-size:15px">How Kodu keeps you safe</b><span class="muted" style="display:block;margin-top:2px">Verification, escrow, disputes and reviews explained.</span></span><button class="btn g sm" style="flex-shrink:0;width:auto" data-htab="policies">Read</button></div>`}
<div class="card col" style="gap:8px"><b style="font-family:Sora,sans-serif;font-size:17px">Still need help?</b><span class="muted">Write in your own language. A person replies within one working day.</span><div class="row" style="gap:8px"><button class="btn p sm" style="flex:1" data-act="helpmsg">${ico("chat","#fff",18)}Message support</button><button class="btn s sm" style="flex:1" data-act="helpcall">Emergency? Call 112</button></div></div>
<div style="height:24px"></div>`};
document.addEventListener("click",e=>{const t=e.target.closest("[data-htab],[data-hpol],[data-act=helpmsg],[data-act=helpcall]");if(!t)return;e.stopPropagation();const d=t.dataset;
 if(d.htab){S.helpTab=d.htab;save();if(route!=="help")go("help");else{render();const s=document.querySelector(".screen");if(s)s.scrollTop=0}return}
 if(d.hpol){S.helpTab="policies";S.helpPol=d.hpol;save();if(route!=="help")go("help");else{render();const s=document.querySelector(".screen");if(s)s.scrollTop=0}return}
 if(d.act==="helpmsg"){toast("Support chat opens here in the real app");return}
 if(d.act==="helpcall"){toast("In an emergency, leave the situation and call 112");return}},true);
document.addEventListener("input",e=>{if(e.target.name!=="hq")return;const q=e.target.value.trim().toLowerCase();let n=0;
 document.querySelectorAll("details.hq").forEach(d=>{const hit=!q||d.textContent.toLowerCase().includes(q);d.style.display=hit?"":"none";if(hit)n++;if(q&&hit)d.open=true;if(!q)d.open=false});
 document.querySelectorAll(".hsec").forEach(s=>{s.style.display=[...s.querySelectorAll("details.hq")].some(d=>d.style.display!=="none")?"":"none"});
 const no=document.querySelector(".hnone");if(no)no.style.display=n?"none":"block"});
(()=>{const st=document.createElement("style");st.textContent=`
details.hq{border-bottom:1px solid #EDE8DF}details.hq:last-child{border-bottom:none}
details.hq summary{list-style:none;display:flex;align-items:center;gap:10px;padding:14px 0;font-size:15px;font-weight:600;cursor:pointer}
details.hq summary::-webkit-details-marker{display:none}
details.hq .hchev{margin-left:auto;display:inline-flex;transition:transform .2s;flex-shrink:0}details.hq[open] .hchev{transform:rotate(45deg)}
details.hq p{margin:-4px 0 14px;font-size:14px;line-height:1.5;color:var(--body)}
`;document.head.appendChild(st)})();
